    10	
    11	## 2. Conventions and complete domains
    12	
    13	Write `z_j` for the unnormalized creation orbital with magnetic quantum number `m=f-j`, `j=0,...,2f`. Its squared one-particle norm is
    14	
    15	`w_j=1/binom(2f,j)=j!/(2f)_j`, with `w_0=1`.
    16	
    17	Here `(x)_s=x(x-1)...(x-s+1)` is the **falling** factorial, with `(x)_0=1`. The Fock inner product is diagonal on monomials:
    18	
    19	`<prod z_j^a_j, prod z_j^b_j> = delta_(a,b) * prod a_j! * w_j^a_j`.
    20	
    21	The normalized creation operator is `a†_(f-j)=z_j/sqrt(w_j)`, and `J_+ z_j=j*z_(j-1)`. We use Condon–Shortley Clebsch–Gordan phases, with the removed spin coupled **first**:
    22	
    23	`|v; i,L,M> = sum_(k,a) r_(i;k,a) [chi_f x |v-1; k,a,L'_k>]_(L,M)`,
