   148	Low-v rules are exact and elementary: retain only existing parent rows and daughter columns from the domain table, and omit absent entire blocks. For example, `v=3` retains row 1 of `X0,X2` and entry `(1,1)` of `X4`; `v=5` retains both parent rows but only column 1 of `X5`. Every retained expression has finite denominators on its domain.
